defmodule NativeEquality do
  # == and != on lists, tuples, options, results, maps, structs and sum types
  # compare structure. The code is made for the type: every piece takes the two
  # values in RDI and RSI, leaves 1 or 0 in AL and may use RAX, RCX, RDX, R8 and
  # R11. A struct or sum type is compared by a function in its table slot, so a
  # type that refers to itself compares by recursion.
  # A call of the comparator in R10: a function's code where it is below
  # 4 GiB, else a function value, whose first word is the code. The code of a
  # position-independent program stands above 4 GiB, less than 1 GiB and the
  # head below the copy of the entry's words (X26, 0x400420 in the program):
  # code is what stands there (spec/darwin-arm64.md).
  def nq_call(): bytes do
